[Options]

[A.]
<h2>More to Take</h2>
<i>^WaR^ Leader: ~wWe need more plans.</i><br>
<i>You: ~wRoger that...I picked up 4 enemies in a custer.</i><br>
<i>^WaR^: ~wNice choice...See those priests in red?  They have more plans then the others to take.</i><br>
Ok...Go in there and kill.

$Button=What you got,ShowTechnology,55
$Button=Start the Fighting,DoNothing,0

[ai2TempleHalfDead]
Here, have this Technology plan, just spare me my temple.
$Button=Sure...why not?,Tell,Help

[Help]
You take the plan and yell sike and continue to bombard the Temple.
$Button=Ha Ha,GetTechnology,79

[ai2TempleDead]
Nimbains, evacuate, she's going to blow...  You run out of the Temple carrying a plan...
$Button=But of what?,GetTechnolgy,136

[ai2PriestDead]
In his robes you find a scroll...
$Button=Read It,Tell,Scroll

[Scroll]
Here's how to make a sun balloon...<br>
1) Get a huge peice of light leather<br>
2) Get a light-weight box<br>
3) Get some string<br>
4) Put them all together<br>
5) Put a fool in the box and promise him glory...<br>
$Button=Cool,GetTechnology,111

[ai5PriestDead]
You find the wind generator.
$Button=Cool,GetTechnology,75

[ai5TempleDead]
Nice work, after leveling the temple you find a plan for Technology.
$Button=Now we are getting somewhere,GetTechnology,129

[ai3PriestDead]
Commander, we have found a Nimbain servant running with this...
$Button=Open it,GetTechnology,87

[ai4PriestDead]
The much needed crossbow was found.
$Button=YES!,GetTechnology,140

[Succeeded][BadTeamDead]
You, Guldan and the ^WaR^ leader come together.
<i>^WaR^ Leader: ~wNow we got plans, we have to make them useful.  Guldan, you take Wind, I will take Rain, and you, chief commander, will take Thunder and Sun.
<i>You: ~wOk
<i>Guldan: ~wSounds good.
<i>^WaR^ Leader: ~wFW...I'm homing in on a target flying to our islands.  Wait...it stopped.  Let's go see what it is doing...
$Button=What's in store for you next?,MissionBegin,FW6

[Failed]
<i>SPU: ~wHa Ha Ha<br>
<i>Mystical Voice: ~wWant a second chance to get back in the war?

$Button=Yes,MissionBegin,FWT2
$Button=No,MissionAbort,0

